## Overview

`service-opentelemetry` uses `Otlp.layerFromConfig()` from `effect/unstable/observability` with `FetchHttpClient` from `effect/unstable/http` to export traces, metrics, and logs over OTLP/HTTP JSON. Effect reads the standard OpenTelemetry environment variables through its configuration layer.

## Layer

```ts
import { Layer } from "effect";
import { FetchHttpClient } from "effect/unstable/http";
import { Otlp, OtlpSerialization } from "effect/unstable/observability";

export const OpenTelemetryLive = Otlp.layerFromConfig().pipe(
  Layer.provide(OtlpSerialization.layerJson),
  Layer.provide(FetchHttpClient.layer),
);
```

### Environment Variables

- `OTEL_SERVICE_NAME` - Service name used in the OpenTelemetry resource
- `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` - Base URL for the OTLP collector
- `OTEL_LOGS_EXPORTER=otlp` - Enables log export
- `OTEL_METRICS_EXPORTER=otlp` - Enables metric export
- `OTEL_TRACES_EXPORTER=otlp` - Enables trace export

Effect leaves each exporter disabled when its corresponding exporter variable is omitted.
